# Bundles and the Marketplace

> Building and deploying your own services to a realm: `beam-build-and-deploy`. Creating the services, storages and portal extensions a bundle carries: `beam-manage-service`, `beam-create-portal-extension`.

## High-Level Architecture

```
 publisher workspace                                   Beamable                                  buyer org
 ───────────────────                                   ────────                                  ─────────
 <name>.beam.bundle.json ─┐
 projects (services,      ├─ bundles plan ─► diff vs latest release
 storages, extensions)  ──┘
                           bundles publish ─► /beamo/releases/upload-targets
                              │  images ─────► marketplace image repos
                              │  files  ─────► signed upload URLs (extension assets, source archives)
                              └─ release ────► /beamo/releases  ─► release vN, tag latest = vN
                                                    │
                                     catalog (/beamo/bundles, /beamo/marketplace)
                                                    │
                                     bundles acquire ─► org library (/beamo/acquisitions)
                                                    │
                                     bundles install ─► /beamo/installations/plan ─► plan + hash
                                                    └► /beamo/installations/apply(hash) ─► zone manifest + realm manifests
                                                    │
                                     auto-update sweep ─► compatible newer releases applied
                                                    │
 bundles source request ─► /beamo/source-deliveries ─► pull request into a connected repository
                                                          (with beam.override.json per project)
 deploy plan/release from that checkout ─► manifest post with overrides ─► local build replaces the bundle's component
```

